# Bandit Level 4 → Level 5 

## Goal
The goal was to locate the password for the next level that is stored in the only human-readable file in the inhere directory

## Commands used
cd inhere
ls
file ./*
cat ./-file07

## Explanation
- 'cd inhere' to change directory into inhere
- 'ls' to list all files in that 'inhere' directory
- 'file' identifies each file's type
- ' ./* ' selects all non-hidden files in this directory and handles names starting with ' - ' and together with ' file ./*' it shows me what file type they are and I can pinpoint which one is the human-readable file in the inhere directory
- 'cat ./-file07' display the content of ' -file07 '

## Result
Was able to pinpoint the human-readable file and use ' cat ' to display the password so I can move onto the next level

## What I learned
I learnt the use case of the ' file ' command and ' ./* ' to go with it so I can bring up the different file type that started with a -
